 Types of Router

 1. Browser Router - Used 99% of the time
    - Uses HTML5 history API (pushState, replaceState and popstate event) to keep your UI in sync/clean with the URL
    - contains -/courses/react -- GOOD for SEO
    - Example: <BrowserRouter></BrowserRouter>

 2. Hash Router
    - Uses the hash portion of the URL (window.location.hash) to keep your UI in sync with the URL
    - contains -/courses.#/react -- NOT GOOD for SEO
    - Example: <HashRouter></HashRouter>

 3. Memory Router
    - Keeps the history of your "URL" in memory (does not read or write to the address bar)
    - Useful in non-browser environments like React Native or tests
    - Example: <MemoryRouter></MemoryRouter>

 4. Static Router (Next.js)
    - Used for server-side rendering
    - Never changes location
    - Example: <StaticRouter location="/somewhere" context={{}}></StaticRouter>


Routes - Container
Route - If URL/path is / then show Home Page


------------------- useNavigate() --------------------

Used for programmatic navigation in React Router

Navigation happens through JavaScript logic, not clicks

Commonly used after login, logout, or form submission

Replaces the older useHistory hook

Can be used only inside functional components



 --------------------- Outlet -----------------

Acts as a placeholder for child routes

Required when implementing nested routing

Parent component must contain Outlet

Child routes render inside the parent layout

Helps create shared layouts (Navbar, Sidebar)

Reduces code duplication

 -------------------  createBrowserRouter -----------------

Modern routing approach introduced in React Router v6.4+

Uses object-based route configuration

Supports nested routes easily

Replaces BrowserRouter and Routes

Used together with RouterProvider

Suitable for large and structured applications


 ------------------- NavLink ----------------------

Special version of Link used for navigation

Automatically detects the active route

Helps apply active styles to links

Commonly used in navigation bars

Improves user experience

Preferred over Link when styling active links